    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7bea208d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: how_to_cook_turkey_in_usa; hasOverallIntent: cultural_comparison; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes two images: the top image shows a whole roasted turkey on a festive table with a Christmas tree in the background, labeled 'how to cook turkey in usa,' implying a traditional, large-scale, holiday meal. The bottom image shows a plated dish of grilled turkey pieces with vegetables and grains, labeled 'how to cook turkey in romania,' suggesting a more casual, modern, or different culinary approach. The overall intent is to humorously contrast American and Romanian turkey preparation styles, using cultural stereotypes or expectations about each country's cuisine. There is no direct targeting of any protected group or harmful content; the humor is based on cultural generalizations, which may be considered mildly offensive or stereotypical but does not meet the threshold of abusive, hateful, or propagandistic intent as defined in the provided knowledge base. The meme relies on the visual contrast and the implied cultural difference to create a comedic effect, not on disparaging any specific group.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_ab4d4ab4"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
